StandardsMap is a plant map of the water system: each zone (generation, storage and distribution, pure steam, controls and data, fabrication, qualification) is a framed area labelled with the standards that govern it, and every code jumps to the row further down the page that proves it.

- Data: block `"type": "standards-map"` with `zones: [{t, codes, to, icon}]`. `to` is the id of the section holding the proof (give that block an `anchor`, or use its nav id `s-N-label`); the zone title jumps there. `codes` are strings as the rows write them ("USP <645>", "EU GMP Annex 1"); a code may be `{t, to}` to point at another section. `icon` is an Icon name, used only when every zone has one (otherwise the `01` index).
- Markup (`blocks/standardsmap.js`): `.aq-standards-map` > `ol.aq-standards-map__zones` (grid; `::before` is the pipe, `::after` its arrow) > `li.aq-standards-map__zone.is-up|is-down` > `.aq-standards-map__head` (Icon `aq-standards-map__icon` or `aq-index`, `h3.aq-standards-map__t` with the section link) and `ul.aq-standards-map__codes` of `a.aq-standards-map__code` (`data-smap-code`, `data-smap-to`).
- Jump: a code chip scrolls to the row naming it (EvidenceMap rows matched on their title, spec and table rows cell by cell, whole-code match so "Annex 1" never lands on "Annex 15"), first in the zone's section, then anywhere on the page. A folded row is unfolded first; the row takes focus and flashes a `flow` outline once (`.aq-standards-map-hit`, no animation under reduced motion).
- Desktop: the first half of the zones above a `flow` pipe header (2 px, arrow at the end), the rest below, each zone a 1 px dashed `line-strong` frame with a `flow` branch and node to the pipe. Codes are mono chips in a 1 px `line-strong` frame with a quiet ↓, `flow` on hover. Phones: zones stacked as compact rows on a vertical pipe at the left, codes wrap as chips.
- Ground: the navy page (a visual anchor ahead of the evidence sheets it indexes). Use only standards the page already lists, each pointing at a row that exists; three to six zones.
- When not to use it: a page citing fewer than about eight standards (a StandardsGrid or the rows themselves say it), or standards with no rows to prove them on the same page.
